Development-time containers (observability/docker-compose.yml)

  The local trace stack is NOT redistributed by Matchbook, is not linked into
  it, and is not required to run anything here: with the stack down,
  observability/instrument.py records nothing and every command still works.
  It is listed because this repository holds its datasets to a stated licence
  and owes its own dependencies the same scrutiny.

  Langfuse            MIT. https://github.com/langfuse/langfuse
                      Its ee/ directory is commercially licensed; unused here.
  ClickHouse          Apache-2.0
  PostgreSQL          PostgreSQL License
  MinIO               AGPL-3.0. Run locally as a separate, unmodified
                      upstream image, which §13 does not reach. Matchbook
                      links no AGPL code -- the reason this repo hand-writes
                      its mining library rather than taking an AGPL one.
  Redis               BSD-3-Clause, pinned at 7.2. Deliberate: Redis 7.4 and
                      later are RSALv2/SSPL, which is not OSI-approved, and
                      taking an upstream compose file unread would have
                      acquired it silently.

